 "answer": "Use **`pg_relation_size()`**, which is a built-in PostgreSQL function, not something pgvector provides. pgvector indexes (HNSW and IVFFlat) are normal index access methods, so it works on them.\n\n```sql\nSELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('my_vector_index'));\n```\n\nRelated functions:\n\n- `pg_indexes_size('my_table')` returns the combined size of all indexes on a table.\n- `pg_total_relation_size('my_vector_index')` includes the index's TOAST and free space map overhead, though for an index this is usually close to `pg_relation_size`.",
